      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The header says `secp256k1_ellswift_create` is constant time in `auxrnd32`, but `ctime_tests` never marks `auxrnd32` secret. Marking it secret makes the test fail under Valgrind and MSan, because `secp256k1_ellswift_xswiftec_inv_var` branches on the branch value and on `u`, which are PRNG outputs derived from `auxrnd32`.\n\nThis declassifies the branch pool and `u32` right after they are drawn, as option 2 in the issue proposes. They are SHA256 outputs, so declassifying them does not reveal `seckey32` or `auxrnd32`. `ctime_tests` now calls `secp256k1_ellswift_create` with both secret.\n\nFixes #1962.\n\n",
